000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. ADVANCE.
000300* WRITE ... AFTER ADVANCING on S/370 is an ASA carriage control
000400* byte in front of the record: the byte says what to do BEFORE the
000500* line prints, which is exactly what AFTER means. ' ' is one line,
000600* '0' two, '-' three, '+' none (overprint) and '1' a new page.
000700* More than three lines is written as blank lines first.
000750* BEFORE holds its advance over to the next line instead, so the
000760* two can add up -- which only the runtime can do, because only
000770* it knows what the last BEFORE left owing.
000800*
000900* GnuCOBOL cannot be the oracle here -- it writes a text file with
001000* newlines rather than control bytes -- so this program is its
001050* own oracle: it writes the file, closes it, reads it back with
001100* the control byte as ordinary data, and displays what it finds.
001300 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001400 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001500 FILE-CONTROL.
001600     SELECT PRT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-PRTFILE.
001700     SELECT RAW-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-PRTFILE.
001800 DATA DIVISION.
001900 FILE SECTION.
002000 FD  PRT-FILE
002100     LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
002200 01  PRT-REC      PIC X(20).
002300 FD  RAW-FILE
002400     LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
002500 01  RAW-REC.
002600     02  R-CTL    PIC X.
002700     02  R-TEXT   PIC X(20).
002800 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
002900 01  EOF-FLAG     PIC X     VALUE 'N'.
003000 01  SEQ          PIC 99    VALUE 0.
003100 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
003200     OPEN OUTPUT PRT-FILE.
003300     MOVE 'PAGE                ' TO PRT-REC.
003400     WRITE PRT-REC AFTER ADVANCING PAGE.
003500     MOVE 'ONE                 ' TO PRT-REC.
003600     WRITE PRT-REC AFTER ADVANCING 1 LINE.
003700     MOVE 'TWO                 ' TO PRT-REC.
003800     WRITE PRT-REC AFTER ADVANCING 2 LINES.
003900     MOVE 'THREE               ' TO PRT-REC.
004000     WRITE PRT-REC AFTER ADVANCING 3 LINES.
004100     MOVE 'OVERPRINT           ' TO PRT-REC.
004200     WRITE PRT-REC AFTER ADVANCING 0 LINES.
004300     MOVE 'FIVE                ' TO PRT-REC.
004400     WRITE PRT-REC AFTER ADVANCING 5 LINES.
004500     MOVE 'DEFAULT             ' TO PRT-REC.
004600     WRITE PRT-REC.
004610     MOVE 'BEFORE2             ' TO PRT-REC.
004620     WRITE PRT-REC BEFORE ADVANCING 2 LINES.
004630     MOVE 'OWES2               ' TO PRT-REC.
004640     WRITE PRT-REC AFTER ADVANCING 1 LINE.
004650     MOVE 'BEFOREPG            ' TO PRT-REC.
004660     WRITE PRT-REC BEFORE ADVANCING PAGE.
004670     MOVE 'AFTERPG             ' TO PRT-REC.
004680     WRITE PRT-REC AFTER ADVANCING 1 LINE.
004700     CLOSE PRT-FILE.
004800     OPEN INPUT RAW-FILE.
004900     PERFORM READ-ONE UNTIL EOF-FLAG = 'Y'.
005000     CLOSE RAW-FILE.
005100     STOP RUN.
005200 READ-ONE.
005300     READ RAW-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF-FLAG.
005400     IF EOF-FLAG NOT = 'Y'
005500         ADD 1 TO SEQ
005600         DISPLAY SEQ ' [' R-CTL '] ' R-TEXT.
